<urn:usf:product-profile-vocabulary-policy:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "v1" <urn:usf:graph:product-profile-vocabulary> .
<urn:usf:product-profile-vocabulary-policy:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "A disposition is a stance, never evidence. Marking a capability current does not assert that it is satisfied; satisfaction is decided from executed evidence alone." <urn:usf:graph:product-profile-vocabulary> .
<urn:usf:product-profile-vocabulary-policy:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "This vocabulary is Core grammar and names no product. It declares no ANQR capability and is usable by any profile realised against this foundation." <urn:usf:graph:product-profile-vocabulary> .
<urn:usf:product-profile-vocabulary-policy:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:objective> "Supply the grammar a product profile needs to state why a capability exists, who it is for, what it observably produces, what would satisfy it and whether the product claims it today." <urn:usf:graph:product-profile-vocabulary> .
<urn:usf:product-profile-vocabulary-policy:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:ownerAuthorityRule> "Core owns the grammar for product meaning; a profile owns every instance stated in it. Core declares no capability of its own here." <urn:usf:graph:product-profile-vocabulary> .
<urn:usf:product-profile-vocabulary-policy:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:CoreSurfacePolicy> <urn:usf:graph:product-profile-vocabulary> .
